The original copyright and permission notice is reproduced verbatim in
LICENSE-MIT-ezf3d. Retain that file when distributing substantial portions of
the adapted implementation.

Adapted areas include ASM header/token framing and analytic geometry layouts,
B-Rep pointer slots, analytic edge sampling, surface inversion, periodic-strip
and monotone-chain tessellation, and Fusion Meta/Bulk stream framing. The Rust reader uses
checked reads, explicit resource limits, section-local ASM pointer indices,
and direct snapshot/body-container component links. It does not embed or call
the Python implementation at runtime.

